pkcs11-proxy (0.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New daemon options to restrict client access: read_only_sessions
    downgrades every session to read-only and reports the token as write
    protected, disabled_functions rejects listed PKCS#11 functions.
  * Configuration file support through PKCS11_PROXY_CONF_PATH with so_path,
    so_recv_timeout, so_keepalive, tcp_keepidle, tcp_keepintvl, tcp_keepcnt,
    psk_file, log_file, read_only_sessions and disabled_functions options.
  * Socket timeout and keepalive options are applied to accepted connections
    so dead peers are detected and their sessions closed.
  * Logging to a file through PKCS11_PROXY_LOG_FILE with timestamps, process
    and thread IDs, and much more detailed debug logging.
  * Version reported by pkcs11-daemon --version and logged on startup by the
    daemon and on C_Initialize by the proxy library.
  * TLS-PSK: TLS 1.2 and newer via TLS_method, custom OpenSSL library
    context, per-thread TLS context, clients receive the identity hint,
    read and write errors and retries handled properly.
  * ECDH: CKM_ECDH1_DERIVE parameters are serialized and the mechanism is
    listed, mechanisms with an IV parameter such as AES CBC pass through.
  * Fix daemon shutdown deadlock and socket handling with connected clients.
  * Fix memory leaks in the call state pool and dispatch state, free the TLS
    state, shrink grown message buffers and use proper allocator functions.
  * Fix dispatcher mutex left locked on accept errors, missing TLS allocation
    check, call state read and write types, segfault in ECDH1_DERIVE
    parameter deserialization and invalid move when purging mechanisms.
  * Fix socket path length to match sun_path and zero its last byte.
  * Add missing seccomp rules and properly disable seccomp when not built in.
  * Build: CMake rewrite requiring CMake 3.10 and OpenSSL 1.1.1, macOS
    support, debug, debug output and optimization options, install targets
    respecting the OS layout, PKCS#11 header updated to 2.40.
  * Python test suite run in CI over TCP and TLS, LICENSE file added,
    p11proxy-mitm moved to tools.

 -- Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:47:32 +0200

